# Build context is the REPO ROOT: `docker build -f deploy/Dockerfile .`, so this file lives here
# and not next to the Dockerfile. BuildKit also honours deploy/Dockerfile.dockerignore, but the
# root form works with every builder, including the one your CI happens to have.
# Keep the API image small and the build cache useful.
.git
.github
archive
demo
docs
tests
*.egg-info
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
*.pyc
kernels/build
dpo_output
dpo_results.json
*.png
*.jpg
# Notebooks are needed only by the kernels image, which un-ignores them explicitly.
*.ipynb
!Agent_Workloads_On_The_Metal.ipynb
!LongContext_KV_Compression_Serving.ipynb
!Serving_WhatIf_Console.ipynb
!Speculative_Decoding_Advanced_Serving.ipynb
!The_Optimization_Stack.ipynb
!Training_Kernels_And_Memory.ipynb
